*---------------------------------------------------------------
* mm.annex2.equ -- aux bank 0 (the kernel annex), PART 2:
* the PCB annex-entry shape and the OFT/pipe object graph
* (docs/MEMMAP.md #2.2, #2.2a).
*
* Split from mm.annex.equ on 2026-08-30 to lower the LARGEST
* SINGLE PUT, which is what real Merlin-8's 41,215 B source
* budget actually charges -- see part 1's header for the formula
* and for what the old "one file, not several" note got
* backwards.
*
* PUT THIS IMMEDIATELY AFTER mm.annex.equ. It references
* names defined there, and real Merlin resolves an `equ` only if
* it was defined before its first reference.
* Full design notes: I.MEMMAPE.TXT (docs/a2/), docs/MEMMAP.md #2
*---------------------------------------------------------------
* -- PCB annex-entry shape (offsets, not addresses -- index by
* entry#) --
*
* TASK #6 RATIFICATION (docs/SCHED.md, docs/TASKS.md #6): task
* #2's PCB_ENTRY was an explicit size RESERVATION, not a real
* field list ("Task #6 (scheduler) owns the real field list --
* treat this as a size reservation, not a struct definition" --
* docs/MEMMAP.md #2.2's original text). The operator's two-
* queue-scheduler ruling requires a PCB_STATE byte AND a
* SEPARATE PCB_WCHAN (wait-channel) byte -- the "everyone else
* is a SET, not a queue" design's whole physical representation
* -- which task #2's placeholder (STATE only, no WCHAN) didn't
* budget for. Ratified here: PCB_ENT_SIZE STAYS 16 (no MEMMAP
* renegotiation needed -- found a fit), by re-scoping
* PCB_CWDINO from a 2-byte raw pointer to a 1-byte INDEX into
* the inode cache (INODE_COUNT=32 fits comfortably in a byte;
* task #11's fs spike owns turning this into a real
* pointer/lookup if a flat index turns out insufficient) -- that
* freed byte is exactly what PCB_WCHAN needed. Keeping the entry
* at a power-of-two size matters mechanically, not just
* aesthetically: sched.s's PCB_PTR_FOR computes PCB_ARRY_ADDR +
* pid*PCB_ENT_SIZE with four ASL/ROL pairs (pid<<4) -- the
* 6502 has no MUL, so a non-power-of-two size would need a real
* shift-and-add multiply on every PCB access (SCH_SWITCH,
* SCH_SLEEP, the SCH_WAKEUP scan's every iteration), not
* just this one boot-time ratification call.
PCB_ENTRY       dum   $0
PCB_PID         ds    1
PCB_STATE       ds    1           ;run-state -- see
                                  ;PCB_UNUSED/PCB_RUNNABLE/ PCB_
                                  ;RUNNING/PCB_BLOCKED/PCB_ZOMBI
                                  ;E below
PCB_WCHAN       ds    1           ;wait channel (task #6
                                  ;ratification) -- 0 = not
                                  ;waiting; meaningful only when
                                  ;PCB_STATE = PCB_BLOCKED.
                                  ;Physically, this byte +
                                  ;PCB_STATE above ARE the
                                  ;"everyone else" set the
                                  ;operator's scheduler ruling
                                  ;describes -- not a separate
                                  ;structure
PCB_BANK        ds    1           ;physical aux bank number for
                                  ;this process
PCB_PARENT      ds    1           ;parent pid
PCB_SAVEDSP     ds    1           ;saved kernel-side SP at last
                                  ;context switch (the annex
                                  ;half of the PCB split -- the
                                  ;per-bank half is BANK_ID +
                                  ;FFXX_SCRATCH in the $FFxx
                                  ;page, docs/MEMMAP.md #3.3;
                                  ;task #6 does not add a second
                                  ;copy there)
PCB_EXITSTAT  ds    1
* -- 2026-08-22: the byte that was PCB_SPARE (and PCB_CWDINO
* -- before that -- an index into the V6 inode cache the ProDOS
* -- ruling deleted; a ProDOS cwd is a PATH and lives in the
* -- annex at CWD_TBL_ADDR, by pid) is now the process BREAK.
* --
* -- PCB_BRK holds the break as a PAGE NUMBER, not an address:
* -- the break is `PCB_BRK * 256`, and the process heap is the
* -- half-open interval [LOAD_BASE, PCB_BRK*256). One byte is
* -- all there was -- PCB_ENT_SIZE must stay 16 so PCB_PTR_FOR
* -- can index with pid<<4 (four ASL/ROL pairs) instead of a
* -- multiply -- and one byte is enough, because a bank copy is
* -- page-granular anyway and $08..$BF spans the whole window.
* -- src/kernel/process.s PRC_BRK rounds every request UP to a
* -- page, so a program never gets LESS than it asked for.
* --
* -- ZERO MEANS "NO BREAK ESTABLISHED", not "an empty heap":
* -- the kernel cannot know where a program's uncleared `dum`
* -- region ends, so the program declares its own initial break
* -- (see docs/MEMMAP.md #3.2b). SCH_CREATE already zeroes this
* -- byte for every new process, so a reused pid can never
* -- inherit the previous occupant's break.
* --
* -- WHY IT IS IN THE PCB and not a main-memory kernel array:
* -- a future fork() copies a LIVE bank, and without a break it
* -- must copy the whole 46848-byte window (~1.83M cycles at
* -- the measured 39.07 cyc/byte, ~1.8s at 1MHz). With one it
* -- copies [LOAD_BASE, PCB_BRK*256) and stops. That read wants
* -- to ride along on the PCB_RD_FIELDS call the spawn path
* -- already makes, in the record that already describes the
* -- process -- not in a second parallel table.
PCB_BRK         ds    1           ;break PAGE (0 = unset)
PCB_FDTABLE     ds    8           ;8 fds/process (HARD LIMIT) --
                                  ;each byte is an OFT_COUNT-
                                  ;range INDEX into the single
                                  ;global Open File Table (OFT)
                                  ;below, 0 = unused slot (never
                                  ;a valid OFT index -- OFT
                                  ;entry 0 is likewise never
                                  ;allocated, see OFT_COUNT
                                  ;below). Task #13 amendment
                                  ;(code review C3):
                                  ;see the OFT object-graph
                                  ;block below this PCB_ENTRY
                                  ;dum for the full, now-
                                  ;implemented model (fd -> OFT
                                  ;index -> pipe slot or ProDOS
                                  ;refnum+iobuf) -- this comment
                                  ;previously just said "index
                                  ;into the global open-file
                                  ;table" with no further
                                  ;detail, docs/MEMMAP.md had
                                  ;none either, and the kernel's
                                  ;real object model had already
                                  ;grown past that one-line
                                  ;description
PCB_ENTRY_LEN   equ   *
            dend
* PCB_ENTRY_LEN must equal PCB_ENT_SIZE above -- both are 16.

* -- PCB_STATE values (task #6 ratification, docs/SCHED.md) --
PCB_UNUSED      equ   0           ;slot never allocated, or
                                  ;freed after reap
PCB_RUNNABLE    equ   1           ;on the run queue, not
                                  ;currently executing
PCB_RUNNING     equ   2           ;currently executing (curbank
                                  ;== PCB_BANK); at most one PCB
                                  ;is ever RUNNING at a time
PCB_BLOCKED     equ   3           ;sleeping on PCB_WCHAN
                                  ;(sched.s SCH_SLEEP/
                                  ;SCH_WAKEUP) -- part of the
                                  ;"everyone else" SET, not the
                                  ;run queue
PCB_ZOMBIE      equ   4           ;exited, awaiting wait() reap
                                  ;-- process- call surface
                                  ;(task #3 scope), not consumed
                                  ;by sched.s's own
                                  ;switch/wakeup logic beyond
                                  ;never scheduling it again
* -- PCB_STOPPED (docs/JOB-CONTROL.md Increment B, 2026-09-08):
* -- suspended by the ^Z sweep (procspawn2.s PRC_STOP_SWP). Not
* -- schedulable, not dead: bank intact, fds open, resumable by
* -- SYS_CONT (STOPPED -> RUNNABLE + RUNQ_PUSH). ITS OWN VALUE,
* -- not "BLOCKED on a magic channel": SCH_WAKEUP matches
* -- PCB_BLOCKED only, so no channel wakeup can ever un-stop a
* -- job. Every PCB_STATE reader weighs it -- sched.s :statechk
* -- (never RUNQ_PUSH a stopped pid: it would be popped and
* -- skipped forever), PRC_WAIT (counts, is not reaped; a
* -- stopped-only child set never blocks), PRC_KILL (alive --
* -- kill -9 works), both sweeps (skipped), and the orphan
* -- adoption (process2.s PRC_ADOPT: a stopped child of a dead
* -- parent can never be continued by it, so init adopts it and
* -- it gets SIGHUP then SIGCONT, ORPHAN-1).
PCB_STOPPED     equ   5

* Inode-cache entry shape REMOVED (task #11 amendment -- see the
* INODE_* removal note above this file's PCB_ENTRY block).

* -- pipe metadata shape (offsets; the 256B ring itself is a
* flat buffer,
*    addressed separately from this fixed-size header) --
* TASK #13 AMENDMENT (code review C3): the `PIPE_META`
* dum block below is SUPERSEDED and commented out (not deleted,
* per this codebase's own INODE_*-removal precedent above) --
* task #12's implementation (`src/kernel/process.s`) does not
* use an array-of-8-byte-structs shape at all. See "2.2a Open
* File Table (OFT) object graph" immediately below for what
* actually replaced it, kept assembling as plain comments so a
* reader who remembers the OLD design can find the pointer to
* the new one rather than the block silently vanishing with no
* trail.
*   PIPE_META       dum   $0
*   PIPE_RDPTR      ds    1
*   PIPE_WRPTR      ds    1
*   PIPE_READER_PID ds    1
*   PIPE_WRITER_PID ds    1
*   PIPE_FLAGS      ds    1
*   PIPE_PAD        ds    3
*   PIPE_META_LEN   equ   *
*               dend
* PIPE_META_LEN must equal PIPE_MT_SIZE above -- both are 8.
* (this comparison is dead along with the struct it checked)

* See I.MEMMAPE.TXT: "2.2a Open File Table (OFT) object"
OFT_COUNT   equ   16               ;HARD LIMIT -- global Open
                                   ;File Table entry count
                                   ;(index 0 never allocated)
OFT_FREE    equ   0                ;OFT_TYPE tag: slot unused
OFT_PIPE_R  equ   1                ;OFT_TYPE tag: pipe read end
OFT_PIPE_W  equ   2                ;OFT_TYPE tag: pipe write end
OFT_FILE    equ   3                ;OFT_TYPE tag: ProDOS-backed
                                   ;file
OFT_BLK     equ   4                ;OFT_TYPE tag: /dev/sNdM
                                   ;block device -- docs/KSEG.md
                                   ;"Cells and equates"
* -- OPEN-RO (docs/OPEN-RO-2-NOTES.md): for an OFT_FILE entry
* -- OFT_PIPE (a pipe index for a pipe end, else unused) holds
* -- four flag bits.
OFTF_RO     equ   $80              ;opened with read intent: may
                                   ;join a peer; WRITE refused
OFTF_MG     equ   $40              ;a member of a shared group:
                                   ;its mark lives in the slot
                                   ;store
OFTF_AP     equ   $20              ;opened with append intent:
                                   ;every WRITE/SET_EOF seeks
                                   ;to EOF first (OAPPEND-1)
OFTF_PIN    equ   $10              ;opened by a RELATIVE path:
                                   ;never a park victim itself
                                   ;(its group may park through
                                   ;an unpinned member)
